From f8e56d34e12250d2a18b5fb177579c99bfd02ecd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:06:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AArch64: scalar floating point and the memory forms real code
 uses; byte/halfword exclusives, CLREX, DSB, prefetches

Stores of vector registers with pre/post index and register offset (B,H,S,D,Q), pair stores of S,D,Q registers
(Q as two 128-bit stores), FCSEL, FCCMP/FCCMPE, FMIN/FMAX/FMINNM/FMAXNM, FNMUL, FMSUB/FNMADD/FNMSUB, FSQRT,
FRINT{N,A,M,P,Z,X,I}, FCVT{N,A,M,P}{S,U}, FCVTZ{S,U} with ARM's saturation (x86 gives 0x80000000 for
everything out of range) and fixed-point forms, SCVTF/UCVTF fixed-point and scalar SIMD forms. An invalid
operation without a NaN operand gives ARM's positive default NaN, not x86's negative one. LDXRB/H, LDAXRB/H,
STXRB/H, STLXRB/H, STLRB/H, CLREX, DSB, PRFM/PRFUM as no-ops.
